<details id="image-editor-panel" class="image-editor-panel"><summary>Add or edit an article image</summary>
<p class="small">Use an existing public HTTPS image URL. Select a Word image placeholder or ordinary article text to replace it, or place a new image at the article end. Paragraph breaks keep the image separate. No image is loaded, uploaded, or checked here.</p>
<div class="actions"><button id="image-use-selection" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use current article selection</button><button id="image-at-end" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Place at article end</button></div>
<div id="image-placeholder-choices" hidden><label for="image-placeholder-select">Omitted Word image to replace</label><select id="image-placeholder-select" aria-describedby="image-placeholder-help"></select><p id="image-placeholder-help" class="small">Numbers are the original article labels, not the remaining image count. Repeated labels can come from combined documents. Compare each occurrence with its original Word document and placement map.</p><label for="image-placeholder-context">Selected occurrence in context</label><textarea id="image-placeholder-context" rows="3" readonly></textarea><button id="image-use-placeholder" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use selected Word placeholder</button><p id="image-placeholder-limit" class="small"></p></div>
<p id="image-target-status" class="small">Choose a location before preparing a change.</p>
<label for="image-target-context">Pinned location in the current article</label><textarea id="image-target-context" rows="3" readonly></textarea>
<details id="image-map-panel"><summary>Match a downloaded Word image package</summary>
<ol class="small"><li>Before importing a Word file, prepare and download its images &amp; placement notes. Extract that ZIP on your device.</li><li>Inspect the recovered files and upload the chosen image in your publishing tool. Original bytes can include metadata and areas hidden by Word cropping. Review them before uploading.</li><li>Open the package's image-map.json below. Use Find next matching Word image to pin a unique editable placeholder, or choose a numbered occurrence manually. Always compare its file, article context, and alternative text against the original Word document. Matching numbers alone do not verify provenance.</li><li>Use the reviewed alternative text or write your own. Paste the uploaded image's public HTTPS URL into Image URL, then preview and apply the change.</li></ol>
<label for="image-map-file">Open image-map.json from the extracted package</label><input id="image-map-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" aria-describedby="image-map-help"><p id="image-map-help" class="small">Only this selected UTF-8 map is read, up to 512 KiB. No image, folder, ZIP, or URL is opened. Map text stays in this tab until cleared or the workspace is replaced; it is excluded from backups, browser recovery, collections, and exports.</p>
<div id="image-map-review" hidden><p id="image-map-scope" class="small"></p><label for="image-map-entry">Placement map entry</label><select id="image-map-entry"></select><p id="image-map-file-note" class="small"></p><label for="image-map-alt">Alternative text supplied in Word</label><textarea id="image-map-alt" rows="3" readonly></textarea><p id="image-map-match" class="small"></p><label class="check"><input id="image-map-confirm" type="checkbox" disabled><span>I compared this entry with the pinned article occurrence and original Word document</span></label><button id="image-map-use-alt" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use reviewed Word alternative text</button></div>
<button id="image-map-clear" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Clear placement map</button><p id="image-map-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">No placement map is open. Entering image details manually is also available.</p>
</details>
<label for="image-url">Image URL (HTTPS)</label><textarea id="image-url" rows="2" inputmode="url" maxlength="2048" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" disabled aria-describedby="image-url-help"></textarea><p id="image-url-help" class="small">A direct image file URL, up to 2,048 characters. No credentials, spaces, or quoted titles. The address is preserved as entered.</p>
<label for="image-alt">Alternative text</label><textarea id="image-alt" rows="2" maxlength="500" disabled aria-describedby="image-alt-help"></textarea><p id="image-alt-help" class="small">Describe the image's purpose in this article, up to 500 characters on one line. For an intentionally decorative image, clear this field and select the option below.</p>
<label class="check"><input id="image-decorative" type="checkbox" disabled><span>This image is decorative and should have empty alternative text</span></label>
<button id="image-preview" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Preview image change</button>
<div id="image-change-preview" hidden><h3>Review the exact replacement</h3><p class="small">Only the selected text is replaced. Added paragraph breaks appear below. The rest of the article is kept exactly.</p><label for="image-before">Selected text to remove</label><textarea id="image-before" rows="3" readonly></textarea><label for="image-after">Markdown to insert, including paragraph breaks</label><textarea id="image-after" rows="4" readonly></textarea></div>
<div class="actions"><button id="image-apply" type="button" class="button" disabled>Apply image change</button><button id="image-discard" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Discard image preparation</button></div>
<p id="image-editor-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Image editor is loading. You can edit Markdown directly.</p>
<p class="small">Applying saves a checkpoint and clears export approval and the linked-image choice. For WordPress, open Images for WordPress and explicitly choose linked Image blocks afterward. Other exports keep image Markdown as text. Unsaved image preparation is excluded from backups, collections, and exports; apply it first to keep it. <a href="/help/publishing-handoff/#image-editor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image editing help (new tab)</a></p>
</details>
